-- T6 regression: an exception raised inside an `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME`
-- scope must not leak the temporal override into subsequent directives.
--
-- Pre-fix, 'raiseException' unwound the frame stack without interpreting
-- the EvalAsOfSystemTime2 restore frame, so the override stayed in the
-- ambient context: directive 3 reported the OVERRIDDEN serial instead of
-- the ambient one, and directive 4 cached a freshly forced shared binding
-- under the leaked context. Fixed by (a) interpreting temporal-restore
-- frames during exceptional unwinding ('unwindFrame' in Machine.hs) and
-- (b) an unconditional ambient-context restore at the directive boundary
-- ('nfDirective').
--
-- The test harness pins the clock: JL4_FIXED_NOW = 2025-01-31T15:45:30Z,
-- so ambient DATE_SERIAL TODAY = 739646; serial of 2000-01-01 = 730484.

TIMEZONE IS "Etc/UTC"

past MEANS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000)

-- expected: 739646 (ambient control)
#EVAL DATE_SERIAL TODAY

-- expected: Division by zero (raised INSIDE the override scope)
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` past (1 DIVIDED BY 0)

-- expected: 739646 (pre-fix leaked 730484 — the override survived the
-- exceptional unwind into this directive)
#EVAL DATE_SERIAL TODAY

fresh MEANS DATE_SERIAL TODAY

-- expected: 739646 (pre-fix the shared binding was forced and cached under
-- the leaked 2000-01-01 context)
#EVAL fresh
